


YPPOLL(8)           UNIX Programmer's Manual            YPPOLL(8)



NAME
     yppoll - what version of a YP map is at a YP server host

SYNOPSIS
     yppoll [ -h _h_o_s_t ] [ -d _d_o_m_a_i_n ] _m_a_p_n_a_m_e

DESCRIPTION
     _y_p_p_o_l_l asks a _y_p_s_e_r_v process what the order number is, and
     which host is the master YP server for the named map. If the
     server is a v.1 YP protocol server, _y_p_p_o_l_l uses the older
     protocol to communciate with it.  In this case, it also uses
     the older diagnostic messages in case of failure.

OPTIONS
     -h _h_o_s_t
          Ask the _y_p_s_e_r_v process at _h_o_s_t about the map parame-
          ters.  If _h_o_s_t isn't specified, the YP server for the
          local host is used.  That is, the default host is the
          one returned by _y_p_w_h_i_c_h(8).

     -d _d_o_m_a_i_n
          Use _d_o_m_a_i_n instead of the default domain.

SEE ALSO
     ypserv(8), ypfiles(5)






























